  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given KKK permutations of integers 111 through NNN. For each iii (1≤i≤K1 \\le i \\le K1≤i≤K), the iii-th permutation is denoted by Ai,1,Ai,2,…,Ai,NA_{i,1}, A_{i,2}, \\ldots, A_{i,N}Ai,1​,Ai,2​,…,Ai,N​.\n\nConstruct a directed acyclic graph with NNN nodes (numbered 111 through NNN) such that:\n\n\nEach of the given permutations is a valid topological sort of the graph. Formally, for each valid kkk and each i,ji, ji,j (1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\le i \\lt j \\le N1≤i&lt;j≤N), there is no edge from the node Ak,jA_{k,j}Ak,j​ to the node Ak,iA_{k,i}Ak,i​.\nThe outdegree of each node is at most 111.\nThe number of nodes with indegree 000 is the smallest possible.\nIf there are multiple solutions, you may find any one.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤5001 \\le N \\le 5001≤N≤500",
      "1≤K≤1001 \\le K \\le 1001≤K≤100",
      "1≤Ai,j≤N1 \\le A_{i,j} \\le N1≤Ai,j​≤N for each valid i,ji,ji,j",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2,0002,0002,000",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (20 points):**",
      "N≤20N \\le 20N≤20",
      "K≤10K \\le 10K≤10"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK.\nKKK lines follow. For each iii (1≤i≤K1 \\le i \\le K1≤i≤K), the iii-th of these lines contains NNN space-separated integers Ai,1,Ai,2,…,Ai,NA_{i,1}, A_{i,2}, \\ldots, A_{i,N}Ai,1​,Ai,2​,…,Ai,N​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print two lines.\n\n\nThe first of these lines should contain one integer ― the minimum number of nodes with indegree 000.\nThe second line should contain NNN space-separated integers v1,v2,…,vNv_1, v_2, \\ldots, v_Nv1​,v2​,…,vN​ describing your graph in the following way: for each valid iii, if vi=0v_i = 0vi​=0, there is no outgoing edge from the iii-th node; otherwise, there is an edge from the iii-th node to the viv_ivi​-th node.",
    "notes": [],
